            }
          ],
          "logprobs": [],
          "text": "**Not necessarily—one typo isn’t an automatic rejection.** It depends on the mistake, the hiring manager, and the role; an editing job may put more weight on it than other positions. ([indeed.com](https://www.indeed.com/career-advice/resumes-cover-letters/typo-on-resume?utm_source=openai))\n\nIf you’ve already submitted it:\n- **Minor spelling or punctuation error:** I’d fix your master copy rather than send an apology just to flag it. Small errors don’t always warrant resubmitting. ([enhancv.com](https://enhancv.com/blog/typo-on-resume/?utm_source=openai))\n- **Wrong contact information or a typo that changes your qualifications:** Send a corrected version with a brief note so they have accurate information. ([resumespice.com](https://resumespice.com/i-submitted-my-resume-with-a-mistake-what-do-i-do/?utm_source=openai))\n- **Portal lets you replace the document:** Upload the corrected copy there. ([indeed.com](https://www.indeed.com/career-advice/finding-a-job/reapply-for-a-job?utm_source=openai))\n\nDon’t count yourself out over this. **What was the typo, and what role are you applying for?**"
        }
